/-!
# Packed inputs for the first native compound matrix

For an original code row `i` and a position `k` in an increasing five-subset,
bit `j` of `columnA i k` is the literal entry of `codeMatrix false` in column
`fiveTuple j k`. Every bit of the table is checked below. This table permits
one packed determinant calculation per exterior row.

`source/generate.py` transcribes the numbers from the published native code
rows. Neither Python nor its output is a proof premise. The row order and
column convention are those of `NativeActions/source/README.md`.
Sources: James, J. Algebra 27 (1973), 57–111; GM02 Proposition 5.1.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Representation.Mathieu.M24DegreeSpectrum.AbsoluteSpectrum.LargeModels.Degree220Pair.NativeActions.ExteriorCoordinates.First

